---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — capital-zone"
  description="Privacy policy for capital-zone, a private read-only Gmail tool built by Stanley Tejakusuma for his own use."
  path="/legal/capital-zone/privacy"
>
  <section class="representative representative--narrow privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-h">
    <p class="mono-label">legal / privacy</p>
    <h1 class="section-heading" id="privacy-h">Privacy — capital-zone</h1>
    <p class="section-copy">
      capital-zone is a private tool Stanley Tejakusuma built for his own use. It is not offered to
      anyone else.
    </p>

    <h2 class="privacy__heading">What it accesses</h2>
    <p class="section-copy">
      With the account owner's consent, read-only access to Gmail (<code>gmail.readonly</code>). It
      reads message details such as sender, subject and date to track the owner's own financial
      accounts. It reads message content only with the owner's explicit approval.
    </p>

    <h2 class="privacy__heading">Where data goes</h2>
    <p class="section-copy">
      It stays on a private server the owner controls. It is never sold, shared, used for
      advertising or used to train AI models.
    </p>

    <h2 class="privacy__heading">Google user data</h2>
    <p class="section-copy">
      Use of data received from Google APIs follows the{' '}
      <a
        class="inline-link"
        href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
        >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
      >, including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2 class="privacy__heading">Revoking access</h2>
    <p class="section-copy">
      Google Account → Security → Your connections to third-party apps &amp; services → capital-zone
      → remove access.
    </p>

    <h2 class="privacy__heading">Contact</h2>
    <p class="section-copy">gstanleytejakusuma@gmail.com · Last updated 9 November 2026</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy__heading {
    margin: 2.2rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
